  "kind": "behavioural",
  "machine": "render",
  "name": "render_a_faulting_program_leaves_what_was_underneath",
  "description": "A device is never dark because of software. A program that faults mid-frame leaves the pixel showing whatever was underneath rather than black, and the fault is reported rather than swallowed - a program that dies every frame is a bug somebody needs to hear about, and the alternative is a strip that is quietly the wrong colour. The high-priority source here divides by zero on every pixel, which is a fault the VM catches at run time rather than a program the loader could have refused.",
